     "en": "Define a register and a shift register"
    },
    {
     "en": "Explain SISO, SIPO, PISO and PIPO registers"
    },
    {
     "en": "Describe ring and Johnson counters and shifting as ×2 and ÷2"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A USB cable sends a byte one bit at a time, but the computer needs all eight bits together. A row of flip-flops that passes bits along on each clock turns serial data into parallel and back.",
