  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Registers and shift registers"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A register is a group of flip-flops that stores a binary word, one bit per flip-flop. In a shift register, D flip-flops are connected in cascade with a common clock: the output of each feeds the D input of the next, so on every clock pulse the stored bits move one place. By the way data enter and leave, there are four types: serial-in serial-out (SISO), serial-in parallel-out (SIPO), parallel-in serial-out (PISO) and parallel-in parallel-out (PIPO). Loading n bits serially needs n clock pulses."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "n-bit register = n flip-flops"
    },
    {
     "en": "SISO, SIPO, PISO, PIPO"
    },
    {
     "en": "Serial loading of n bits needs n clock pulses"
    },
    {
     "en": "Universal shift register (IC 74194): shift left/right, parallel load"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A shift register is a chain of D flip-flops with a common clock. On each clock pulse every bit moves one place, so n bits enter serially in n clock pulses.",
    "kn": "ಶಿಫ್ಟ್ ರಿಜಿಸ್ಟರ್ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ ಕ್ಲಾಕ್ ಇರುವ D ಫ್ಲಿಪ್-ಫ್ಲಾಪ್‌ಗಳ ಸರಪಳಿ. ಪ್ರತಿ ಕ್ಲಾಕ್ ಪಲ್ಸ್‌ಗೆ ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದು ಬಿಟ್ ಒಂದು ಸ್ಥಾನ ಸರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ; n ಬಿಟ್‌ಗಳಿಗೆ n ಪಲ್ಸ್‌ಗಳು."
   }
  },
