  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Uses: conversion, arithmetic and ring counters"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "SIPO converts serial data to parallel and PISO converts parallel to serial (used in serial communication). Shifting a binary number one place left multiplies it by 2; shifting right divides it by 2. Feeding the last output back to the first input makes a ring counter: with n flip-flops it circulates a single 1 through n states (MOD-n). Feeding back the complement $\\bar{Q}$ of the last stage gives a Johnson (twisted-ring) counter with 2n states (MOD-2n)."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "SIPO: serial → parallel; PISO: parallel → serial"
    },
    {
     "en": "Shift left = ×2, shift right = ÷2"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ring counter: n states; Johnson counter: 2n states"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Shift registers convert serial data to parallel and back. Shifting left doubles a number. A ring counter with n flip-flops has n states and a Johnson counter has two n states.",
    "kn": "ಶಿಫ್ಟ್ ರಿಜಿಸ್ಟರ್ ಸರಣಿ-ಸಮಾಂತರ ಪರಿವರ್ತನೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ. ಎಡಕ್ಕೆ ಸರಿಸಿದರೆ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ದ್ವಿಗುಣ. n ಫ್ಲಿಪ್-ಫ್ಲಾಪ್‌ಗಳ ರಿಂಗ್ ಕೌಂಟರ್‌ಗೆ n ಸ್ಥಿತಿಗಳು, ಜಾನ್ಸನ್ ಕೌಂಟರ್‌ಗೆ 2n."
   }
  },
